{"anchor": {"begin": [15, 0, 414.0], "end": [15, 0, 698.67], "env": "theorem", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 2, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "3.1", "source_sha256": "1b30b24bb36fd23f4c2a044ef9c6d7a3efb72e5b0ae0d30576d3d2befd3f0b1e", "statement": "Theorem 3.1. There are constants 0 < h < 1/100, q ∗ > 0, 0 < X a < X ext < ∞ , and smooth fields on Ω ∗ = {(x, t) : τ > 0, q < q ∗ } with the following properties. (i) There is a vector potential A and an axisymmetric scalar B such that u = curl A + Be θ . (3.3) Both A and Be θ are smooth in Cartesian coordinates at the axis. The field is exactly divergence- free. (ii) Every Cartesian space-time derivative of A, Be θ , p is uniformly bounded on compact spatial subsets with c ≤ q ≤ c ′ < q ∗ , for each 0 < c < c ′ , up to the one-sided boundary τ = 0. The resulting limits of the derivatives are compatible under spatial and time differentiation. (iii) For every α , b, N and every finite X 1 , | ∂ α x ∂ b t R (u, p)| ≤ C α ,b,N,X 1 q N (0 ≤ X ≤ X 1 , q ↓ 0). (3.4) For X ≥ X ext the residual is identically zero, and A = 0, B = K(r, τ ), p = − ∫︂ ∞ r K( ρ , τ ) 2 ρ d ρ , K(r, τ ) = r −1−2h H ext ( τ /r 2 ). (3.5) Here H ext is smooth on [0, ∞ ), with each fixed derivative bounded. The radial swirl heat equation satisfied by K is − ∂ τ K = ∂ 2 r K + r −1 ∂r K − r −2 K.", "title": null}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code)", "confidence": "medium", "coverage": "full", "note": "local_theorem states (i)–(iv) for one set of fields (smooth on all of t < 1, endpoint compatibility as smooth one-sided extensions at every x ≠ 0, the (3.6) asymptotic as |τ^A u_θ − e0| ≤ Cτ^(2h)), with the exterior swirl given as an explicit heat field. The RadialHeatProfile lemmas state that this field has the form r^(−1−2h) H(τ/r²) with H smooth on [0, ∞) and bounded derivatives, and that it solves −∂τ K = ∂²_r K + r^(−1) ∂